          "path": "skills/hooks_file_guard/main.go",
          "lineNumber": 171,
          "lineContent": "if err := boardStore.Reserve(ctx, \u0026reservation); err != nil {",
          "title": "Create reservation for this actor",
          "description": "Reserves file for current actor with TTL when no conflicts exist"
        },
        {
          "id": "6g",
          "path": "skills/hooks_file_guard/main.go",
          "lineNumber": 250,
          "lineContent": "data := map[string]any{",
          "title": "Emit envelope with hook output",
          "description": "Wraps hooks.Output in envelope format and writes to stdout for skill runner to parse"
        }
      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "File Guard Hook Skill Execution Flow\n├── Skill entry point receives Input \u003c-- 6a\n│   ├── Filter: check if write operation \u003c-- 6b\n│   │   └── toolutil.IsWriteOperation() \u003c-- skills/hooks_file_guard/main.go:49\n│   ├── Extract file path from tool JSON \u003c-- 6c\n│   │   └── pathutil.ExtractPath() \u003c-- skills/hooks_file_guard/main.go:86\n│   ├── Query blackboard for conflicts \u003c-- 6d\n│   │   └── boardStore.CheckConflicts() \u003c-- skills/hooks_file_guard/main.go:110\n│   ├── Decision branch: conflict exists? \u003c-- skills/hooks_file_guard/main.go:118\n│   │   ├── YES → Block with reason \u003c-- 6e\n│   │   │   └── hooks.Output{Decision: Block} \u003c-- skills/hooks_file_guard/main.go:124\n│   │   └── NO → Create reservation \u003c-- 6f\n│   │       └── boardStore.Reserve() \u003c-- skills/hooks_file_guard/main.go:171\n│   └── Emit envelope to stdout \u003c-- 6g\n│       └── skillout.Emit() → JSON envelope \u003c-- skills/hooks_file_guard/main.go:253\n└── Skill runner parses stdout \u003c-- internal/hooks/skill_runner.go:65\n    └── Returns Output to dispatcher \u003c-- internal/hooks/skill_runner.go:75",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nIn multi-agent systems, **concurrent file modifications create conflicts** when multiple agents try to edit the same file simultaneously. The file guard hook skill solves this by implementing a **reservation system** that detects and prevents edit conflicts before they occur [6d]. When an agent attempts a write operation, the hook checks if another agent has reserved that file, either **blocking the operation** (strict mode) or **warning about the conflict** (advisory mode) [6e].\n\n## Details\n\n### Hook Skill Entry Point\n\nThe file guard skill is invoked as a **PreToolUse hook** whenever tools are about to execute [6a]. It receives a `hooks.Input` struct containing the event context, tool information, and session metadata.\n\n### Write Operation Filtering\n\nThe skill first filters out non-write operations using **cross-platform tool classification** [6b]. This checks tool names (like `Edit`, `Write` from Claude Code), canonical names (like `edit.apply_patch`, `fs.write_file`), and explicit tool kinds to determine if the operation modifies files.\n\n### File Path Extraction\n\nThe skill extracts the target file path from the tool's JSON input arguments [6c]. The `pathutil.ExtractPath()` function checks common field names (`file_path`, `path`, `file`, `current_path`) to handle different tool schemas.\n\n### Conflict Detection\n\nThe core logic queries the **blackboard store** to check for existing reservations [6d]. It passes the workspace ID, file path, actor ID, and reservation mode (exclusive) to `CheckConflicts()`, which returns any conflicting reservations held by other agents.\n\n### Decision Logic\n\nIf conflicts exist, the hook makes a decision based on the configured mode [6e]:\n- **Strict mode**: Returns a `DecisionBlock` output with conflict details, preventing the tool from executing\n- **Advisory mode**: Returns a `DecisionApprove` with warning context, allowing the operation but informing the agent\n\nIf no conflicts exist, the hook **creates a reservation** for the current actor [6f], claiming the file with a default 10-minute TTL and linking it to the active task.\n\n### Output Emission\n\nThe skill wraps its `hooks.Output` (containing decision, reason, context, and metadata) in an **envelope format** and writes it to stdout [6g]. The skill runner parses this JSON envelope to extract the hook output and return it to the dispatcher for merging with other hooks."
    }
  ],
  "description": "This codemap traces the hook system's event-driven architecture from configuration loading through dispatch, matching, skill execution, and output merging. Key flows include config loading at startup [1a-1f], event dispatch with matcher filtering [2a-2g], skill-backed execution via the runner framework [3a-3g], tool execution integration [4a-4f], deterministic output merging [5a-5g], and a complete hook skill example [6a-6g].",
  "mermaidDiagram": "graph TB\n    subgraph Config[\"Configuration System\"]\n        1a[\"1a: Load config from paths\"]\n        1b[\"1b: Resolve config file paths\"]\n        1c[\"1c: Load and parse YAML\"]\n        1d[\"1d: Convert to HookDef\"]\n        1e[\"1e: Build event index\"]\n        1f[\"1f: Create dispatcher\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Dispatch[\"Dispatch System - Central Hub\"]\n        2a[\"2a: Dispatch hook event\"]\n        2b[\"2b: Lookup hooks by event\"]\n        2c[\"2c: Filter by matchers\"]\n        2d[\"2d: Match tool name\"]\n        2e[\"2e: Extract file path\"]\n        2f[\"2f: Execute matched hook\"]\n        2g[\"2g: Merge outputs\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Execution[\"Skill Execution System\"]\n        3a[\"3a: Resolve skill manifest\"]\n        3b[\"3b: Serialize input to JSON\"]\n        3c[\"3c: Execute skill via executor\"]\n        3d[\"3d: Delegate to runtime\"]\n        3e[\"3e: Create exec runner\"]\n        3f[\"3f: Parse skill stdout\"]\n        3g[\"3g: Extract decision\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Merge[\"Output Merge System\"]\n        5a[\"5a: Merge outputs\"]\n        5b[\"5b: Track block decisions\"]\n        5c[\"5c: Apply last-wins\"]\n        5d[\"5d: Collect contexts\"]\n        5e[\"5e: Concatenate actions\"]\n        5f[\"5f: Join contexts\"]\n        5g[\"5g: Apply priority rules\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Tool[\"Tool Execution Integration\"]\n        4a[\"4a: Execute tool via runner\"]\n        4b[\"4b: Dispatch PreToolUse\"]\n        4c[\"4c: Check if blocked\"]\n        4d[\"4d: Apply mutations\"]\n        4e[\"4e: Execute actual tool\"]\n        4f[\"4f: Dispatch PostToolUse\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph Skills[\"Hook Skill Implementation\"]\n        6a[\"6a: Skill entry point\"]\n        6b[\"6b: Filter non-write ops\"]\n        6c[\"6c: Extract file path\"]\n        6d[\"6d: Check conflicts\"]\n        6e[\"6e: Block on conflict\"]\n        6f[\"6f: Create reservation\"]\n        6g[\"6g: Emit envelope\"]\n    end\n\n    1a --\u003e 1b --\u003e 1c --\u003e 1d --\u003e 1e --\u003e 1f\n    1f --\u003e|provides config| 2b\n    1e --\u003e|indexes events| 2b\n\n    4a --\u003e|initiates| 4b\n    4b --\u003e|sends event| 2a\n    4f --\u003e|sends event| 2a\n\n    2a --\u003e 2b\n    2b --\u003e 2c\n    2c --\u003e 2d\n    2c --\u003e 2e\n    2d --\u003e 2f\n    2e --\u003e 2f\n    2f --\u003e|executes| 3a\n    2f --\u003e|collects outputs| 2g\n\n    3a --\u003e 3b --\u003e 3c --\u003e 3d --\u003e 3e\n    3e --\u003e|returns stdout| 3f --\u003e 3g\n    3g --\u003e|output| 2g\n\n    2g --\u003e|merges| 5a\n    5a --\u003e 5b\n    5b --\u003e 5c\n    5c --\u003e 5d\n    5d --\u003e 5e\n    5e --\u003e 5f\n    5f --\u003e 5g\n    5g --\u003e|result| 4c\n\n    4c --\u003e|approved| 4d --\u003e 4e\n    4e --\u003e|completes| 4f\n\n    3a --\u003e|resolves to| 6a\n    6a --\u003e 6b --\u003e 6c --\u003e 6d\n    6d --\u003e|conflict found| 6e\n    6d --\u003e|no conflict| 6f\n    6e --\u003e 6g\n    6f --\u003e 6g\n    6g --\u003e|stdout| 3f\n\n    style Config fill:#ffec99\n    style Dispatch fill:#a5d8ff\n    style Execution fill:#fcc2d7\n    style Merge fill:#b2f2bb\n    style Tool fill:#99e9f2\n    style Skills fill:#d0bfff"
